      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.The original test has many unused imports, unused class fields, and no explanatory context for the focused test. I'll write a clean version with only what's needed.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused imports (Month constants, ChronoField constants, serialization classes, etc.), drops the two unused fields (`MAX_LENGTH`, `PARIS`), and adds a concise class-level Javadoc and an inline comment explaining *why* `DateTimeException` is expected — making the test's intent immediately clear without changing any runtime behavior."
